# event-kinds — the event taxonomy: every kind a spira_event call site may emit, one per
# line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Read by spira-lint's event-taxonomy rule.
#
# A typo'd kind is refused at send time; catching it at the gate is the difference between
# a taxonomy and free text. Adding a kind is a deliberate act: add it here. Each kind is
# lowercase dotted segments of [a-z0-9], at most 32 characters (the events table column).
aeon.claimed
bead.landed
bead.poisoned
bead.reopened
branch.reclaimed
ci.failed
pilgrimage.complete
note
aeon.rapid
queue.abandoned
